/// `archive`: the final reports of workers this pool already retired.
pub(super) const TEXT: &str = "`mini-swe-mcp archive [--group <group>] [--last <n>]` reads the compact archive of retired workers' final REPORTs. Merging a worker, landing the consolidator that integrated it, discarding one or letting its retention expire all delete the row, the conversation and the branch - and with them the before/after measurements the run put in its REPORT. Every retirement therefore appends ONE line to `<hub dir>/archive.jsonl` first: worker id, owner, group, the task's first line, the final status, whether the verify gate passed, the four REPORT fields (done/files/tests/risks), the merge commit where one is known, the time and the reason it left (merged, integrated, absorbed, discarded or expired). No diffs and nothing else are kept. The file is owner-only (0600) and rotates to archive.jsonl.1 past its size cap, so a long-running hub keeps two generations. The verb is owner-scoped like `list`: you see your own retired workers, `--admin` sees every owner's. `--group` keeps one round, `--last <n>` keeps the N most recently retired.";
